    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 276 tests, 0 failures.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the daily owner-creation limit: creating an owner is now rejected with **400** once 20 owners already share the new owner's registration date (which defaults to today).\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection pattern:\n\n**New pipeline step** \u2014 `EnforceOwnerDailyLimit.java` counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the new owner's, and throws `OwnerDailyLimitException` when the count reaches 20.\n\n**Checked exception + handler** \u2014 `OwnerDailyLimitException` (extends `Exception`) and `OwnerDailyLimitExceptionHandler`, which responds `400 Bad Request` with a `ProblemDetail` body, mirroring the existing `OwnerConflictException` (409) pair.\n\n**Escalation wiring** \u2014 `officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.OwnerDailyLimitException.yml` maps the exception to its handler.\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 inserted `enforceDailyLimit` into `owners.POST.yml` (after `ensureUnique`, before `normalizeCity`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`), so the limit is enforced before the owner is persisted.\n\n**Test** \u2014 `createOwnerRejectedWhenDailyLimitReached` posts 20 owners (each `201 Created`), then asserts the 21st returns `400`.\n\nOne design note worth surfacing: I keyed the limit on the owner's **registration date** rather than a wall-clock \"created today\" timestamp, since the model has no separate creation timestamp and the spec explicitly qualified it \"(by registration date)\". For a normal create (no registration date in the body) `BuildOwner` defaults it to today, so this is exactly \"20 owners registered today.\"",
